# S8 — progress-denominators (ai-tutor), census docs/PICT_CENSUS.md § S8.
# See tests/models/progress-denominators.oracle.ts for the oracle spec.
#
# Drift contract across three independent implementations:
# calculateCourseProgress / calculateModuleProgress / calculateLessonProgress
# (apps/extensions/ai-tutor/server/src/services/progressCalculation.js).
# `Scope` (course/module/lesson) is deliberately NOT a dimension here, for the
# same reason `Path` isn't one in tests/models/material-visibility.pict: as a
# PICT factor it would route each row to exactly one implementation, so no
# row would ever compare two scopes against the same seeded activity — the
# opposite of a drift contract. Instead every row is exercised against all
# three functions in the world-builder
# (apps/extensions/ai-tutor/server/tests/integration/progress-denominators.pict.test.js),
# which cross-products Scope itself. (Static read estimated 4 dims including
# Scope as a factor; re-tiered to 3 real PICT dims once the oracle made clear
# Scope belongs in the world-builder cross-product instead — docs/PICT_CENSUS.md § S8.)
LessonPublished:  yes, no
ModulePublished:  yes, no
AttemptPattern:   not_attempted, correct_only, incorrect_only, correct_then_incorrect, incorrect_then_correct
